  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict and safe. S2 keeps 55°C and a 5% benchmark but does not automatically stop sales above 5%, and gives exact per-model results to customers (not the public), making it weakened on the sales-stop rule. S3 requires new units by 1 Jan 2028 (assumed 12 months) and retrofit within 6 years with an alternative if infeasible. S4 requires built-in suppression in 36 months with equivalent allowed. S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt notices and no transition."
